Group III—The Senses.

Giving Sight, Speech and Hearing.

Subdivisions:—1.

The two blind men;

(a) place, Capernaum;

(b) ref., Matt.

ix.—2.

The man born blind;

{a) place, Jerusalem; (b) ref,

John ix.

3. The blind man;

(a) place, Bethsaida;

(b) ref, Mark viii.

4. The deaf-mute;

(a) place, Decapolis;

(b) ref, Mark viii.

5.

Blind Bartimaeus;

(a) place, Jericho;

(b) ref, Matt, xx; Mark x; Luke xviii.

Self-review;—1. Relate the second miracle of this lecture.

2.

Describe the case of giving sight in miracle three, this lecture.

3. Show that the Savior did not perform these miracles to get honor of men.

4.

Narrate miracle five of this lecture.

5.

Relate a case of healing in your own experience by the direct power of the Priesthood.

